
# <type>[optional scope]: <summary>
# summary: max 50 chars, imperative mood ("add", not "added"), no period.
#
# Remember about a blank line between the title and the body.

# Body: WHAT changed and WHY - not HOW. Wrap lines at 72 chars.
# Delete this section if the summary already says everything.
#
# |--------------------- body: wrap at 72 chars ----------------------|


# Footer (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the break and migration>
#   Refs: #<issue>
#
# ---- Types ----
# feat      new user-facing capability
# fix       bug fix
# perf      performance improvement
# refactor  code change that is neither feat nor fix
# test      adding or fixing tests only
# build     dependencies, toolchain (e.g. uv)
# docs      documentation only
# chore     maintenance, housekeeping, configuration
# ci        CI/CD configuration
# style     formatting only, no logic
#
# ---- Vistea scopes ----
# vision | calibration | activation | gestures | suggestions
# appearance | workarea | ui | interaction | logging | evaluation 
# tests | scripts | deps | core
#
# Rules: lowercase summary, no trailing period, ONE logical change
# per commit. If the summary needs "and", split the commit.